<br><br>
<font class="blocknum">1.</font><font class="step">&nbsp;&nbsp;Risk Categories</p>
<p class="help">The Risk Category relates to a risk level that is indicative of how much risk is being incurred - Risk level 1 being the lowest risk, and risk level 4 being the highest risk. The following table defines each risk category. </p>
<table cellpadding=4 cellspacing=2 class="border" width="100%">
<tr>
	<td class="border">Risk Level</td>
	<td class="border">Category</td>
	<td class="border">Description</td>
</tr>
<!--- Risk Level 1 --->
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top" rowspan=3>1</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">Award Fees </td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Based on performance against contract, a score is provided. This score affords a level of confidence and about  the likelihood of receiving funding. For example, the total contract is worth a million, and our score is 75%, we can be assured of receiving $750,000.
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">Mod Pending (Incremental Funding)</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Incremental funding in current POP and contract. Funding is covered within contract. However, spending of funds is  ahead of schedule. For example, the overall contract is for 1Million, and the expected expenditure to date was expected to be 800K, but is instead 900K.
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top">Internally Cleared</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	HII may need to move money from one project to another. Externally, the client doesn't care, but internally we need to understand how funds are being redistributed. For example, say we have 2 CLINS to accomplish ARA - 50% programming, 50% for reports, and we need to change that allocation.
</td>
</tr>

<!--- Risk Level 2 --->
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top" rowspan=2>2</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">MOD PENDING 
Exercise Option Period
</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Example: The total amount is 2 Million. You plan to spend 1M the first period, and 1M the second period. The first period is in progress and you are getting approval for the next period  as well as increase the overall amount of the contract.
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" vaign="top">COMMERCIAL AT RISK</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Non-government. Documents will be required that cover the intention of the client to pay us.
</td>
</tr>

<!--- Risk Level 3 --->
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top" rowspan=2>3</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">CHANGE IN SCOPE</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	The boundaries and expected work products of the project have increased.
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" vaign="top">Fixed Price Mod</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Fixed price contracts with the government have the greatest amount of risk or the greatest amount of profit. There are also difficult to get changed.
</td>
</tr>

<!--- Risk Level 4 --->
<tr>
	<td class="border" valign="top" rowspan=2>4</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">MOD PENDING <br>(Not Exercise Option Period)</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Funding has not been promised for the period.
</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="border" vaign="top">Pre-Contract Costs</td>
	<td class="border" valign="top">
	Contract has not been awarded.
</td>
</tr>

</table>
	
